TaskFlow database migrations
============================

Alembic was introduced after the project already had a schema, so revision
``0001_initial_schema`` is a baseline of the pre-soft-delete tables and
``0002_add_task_deleted_at`` adds the new nullable column.

Normal upgrade:

    alembic upgrade head

By default ``alembic/env.py`` uses the same database URL as ``database.py``.
To run migrations against a disposable database, set ``TASKFLOW_DATABASE_URL``:

    TASKFLOW_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:///path/to/test.db alembic upgrade head

An existing database that already has the baseline tables (but no
``alembic_version`` table) should be adopted once with:

    alembic stamp 0001_initial_schema
    alembic upgrade head

Do not stamp a legacy database that predates the current schema without first
running the ownership migration in ``migrate_task_ownership.py``.
